# Functional test: an operator rejects one ICMP type and permits another with
# `vpn ipsec policy`, and reads both back from the REAL kernel SPD.
# Spec: plan/release/fixes/spec-rfc4301-architecture-gaps.md (RFC 4301 Section
#       4.4.1.1 ICMP type and code selector; Sections 6.1.1 and 6.1.2, the per-type
#       control over unauthenticated ICMP; user story 3). The listing is documented
#       in docs/architecture/ike/ipsec-dataplane-inspection.md.
#
# VALIDATES: two operator entries reach the kernel exactly and read back through
#            `show vpn ipsec dataplane policy` (ze-ike RPC -> ListPolicies ->
#            policyInfoFromKernel -> policyInfoToMap):
#              - unreach-in: action discard, direction in, protocol 1, icmp-type 3
#                (Destination Unreachable), icmp-code 0-3. The code range 0..3 is
#                one mask-aligned block (dataplane.MaskedBlocks), so the kernel holds
#                type 3 exact (icmp-type "3") and code 0 under mask 0xfffc
#                (icmp-code "0/0xfffc"), at the priority its order wrote (800), with
#                the remote prefix as the source and the local prefix as the
#                destination of the inbound packet;
#              - echo-reply-in: action bypass, direction in, protocol 1, icmp-type 0,
#                code any, at priority 801.
# PREVENTS: an ICMP selector widened to every type or code (a DISCARD that eats
#           every ICMP message), a code range narrowed or split wrongly, and a type
#           written into the wrong half of the selector port pair.
#
# DEPENDS ON the icmp-type and icmp-code keys of `show vpn ipsec dataplane policy`
# (cmd/show_dataplane.go policyInfoToMap), added beside the raw src-port/dst-port
# columns for a protocol 1 or 58 row, and on the operator icmp-type/icmp-code leaves
# (ipsec/spd_policy.go parseICMPSelector). Both land with the same RFC 4301 work.
#
# WHY ONE DAEMON. The operator entries are installed on the first configuration
# apply (apply.go -> installSPDPolicies) with no tunnel involved. The site-to-site
# peer is connection-type respond and nobody initiates, so no Child SA ever runs:
# it is there only so the ike engine has a peer to serve.
#
# WHY unmatched bypass. Written, so the start-time Error of the default discard
# (warnImplicitDiscardAtStart) stays out of the subject, and so the catch-all does
# not cut the namespace this test runs in.
#
# WHY THESE PREFIXES. The entries are node-wide for the life of the test, so they
# use RFC 2544 benchmarking ranges (198.18.244.0/23) no other ipsec test installs.
#
# WHY EACH ASSERTION BINDS ITS KEYS ON ONE ROW. A row's JSON keys are sorted
# (action, direction, dst, dst-port, icmp-code, icmp-type, if-id, if-index, mode,
# owner, owner-known, priority, reqid, role, spd, src, src-port, tunnel-dst,
# tunnel-src, upper-proto), and no value of a row is an object, so `[^}]*` keeps
# one match inside one row. The ` ?` takes compact and indented JSON alike.
#
# RED PROOF: in internal/component/ike/engine/spd_policy.go spdICMPMatches, delete
# `typ = dataplane.ExactPortMatch(uint16(p.ICMP.Type))`. The type stays ANY, both
# rows read icmp-type "any", and both matches= assertions fail. A second break,
# `return []spdICMPMatch{{typ: typ, code: dataplane.AnyPortMatch()}}` hoisted above
# the HasCode test, widens the code range to any and the first assertion fails.
#
# Gated option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf: the daemon programs real XFRM
# policies, so this SKIPs on a host without CAP_NET_ADMIN and runs as root in the
# QEMU VM, where `fsuite ipsec` in internal/le/test/qemu/alltests.go executes it.

# bpf: the default `vpn ipsec application-override deny` loads a cgroup setsockopt guard.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,bpf
# Serialize against every other real-XFRM ipsec test: the SPD is NODE-WIDE.
option=exclusive:group=ipsec-xfrm
option=env:var=ze_test_ike_port:value=$PORT2
option=timeout:value=90s
option=env:var=ze_log_ike:value=info

stdin=daemon:terminator=EOF_DAEMON
plugin {
	external engine-steps {
		run "le mock engine-steps ./engine-steps.json"
		encoder json
	}
}

vpn {
	ipsec {
		unmatched bypass
		policy unreach-in {
			action discard
			order 800
			direction in
			protocol 1
			icmp-type 3
			icmp-code 0-3
			local {
				prefix 198.18.244.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.245.0/24
			}
		}
		policy echo-reply-in {
			action bypass
			order 801
			direction in
			protocol 1
			icmp-type 0
			local {
				prefix 198.18.244.0/24
			}
			remote {
				prefix 198.18.245.0/24
			}
		}
		esp-group esp-default {
			lifetime 3600
			proposal 1 {
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		ike-group ike-default {
			key-exchange ikev2
			lifetime 28800
			proposal 1 {
				dh-group 14
				encryption aes256
				hash sha256
			}
		}
		site-to-site {
			peer idle {
				ike-group ike-default
				esp-group esp-default
				connection-type respond
				local-address 127.0.0.2
				remote-address 127.0.0.1
				mode tunnel
				traffic-selector 1 {
					local {
						prefix 198.18.246.0/24
					}
					remote {
						prefix 198.18.247.0/24
					}
				}
				authentication {
					mode pre-shared-secret
					pre-shared-secret test-key-1234
				}
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_DAEMON

# The daemon carries the executor: the engine steps end with `request shutdown`, so
# this process exits when they are done.
cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze -:stdin=daemon:timeout=80s

# ── Engine steps, dispatched inside the daemon ──

command=show vpn ipsec dataplane policy | json
# The rejected type: discard, inbound, type 3 exact, codes 0..3 as one block, at
# the order the operator wrote, sourced from the remote prefix.
expect=output:matches="action": ?"discard",[^}]*"direction": ?"in",[^}]*"dst": ?"198\.18\.244\.0/24",[^}]*"icmp-code": ?"0/0xfffc",[^}]*"icmp-type": ?"3",[^}]*"priority": ?800,[^}]*"role": ?"operator",[^}]*"src": ?"198\.18\.245\.0/24":timeout=30
# The permitted type: bypass, inbound, type 0 exact, every code.
expect=output:matches="action": ?"bypass",[^}]*"direction": ?"in",[^}]*"dst": ?"198\.18\.244\.0/24",[^}]*"icmp-code": ?"any",[^}]*"icmp-type": ?"0",[^}]*"priority": ?801,[^}]*"role": ?"operator",[^}]*"src": ?"198\.18\.245\.0/24":timeout=10

expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=engine-steps: all steps passed
reject=stderr:pattern=could not install operator SPD policy
reject=stderr:pattern=panic recovered
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
